      "problem": "The linear form $f(\\mathbf{x})$ is defined as $f(\\mathbf{x}) = \\mathbf{a} \\mathbf{x},$ where ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14124253/assets/af5a3add30b403955409fc5c9315f2607a432461e85e4b129e37e0f8e55245a9.svg)  Evaluate the function when ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14124253/assets/aee097401481134f5802be4cba03f62ff46cf5fd0f4860fc85e7a85596d3ae09.svg)",
      "worked_solution": "Substituting ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14124253/assets/8d6326ecf66d2e20be5893c256b05f45cf986f00aa332e5b2e343a79096af202.svg) we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =ax \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 & 4\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 8 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =3\\cdot (-5)+0\\cdot 8+4\\cdot 5 \\\\  & =-15+0+20 \\\\  & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
